    "summary": "Emotional Days Between & lively Iko Iko amid mixed set energy",
    "blurb": "The show shines on the soaring Days Between and a spirited Iko Iko, with strong second‑set moments like That Would Be Something into Throwing Stones. First‑set energy wanes mid‑show but recovers later, delivering solid versions of Row Jimmy, Picasso Moon and Truckin'. Overall a mixed‑energy performance with several standout gems.",
    "review": "October 2, 1994 at the Boston Garden captured a night that oscillated between highs and lows. After a powerful opening stretch – Jack Straw, Loser, and a punchy Row Jimmy – the band slipped into a flatter middle before pulling themselves together in the second set. The real jewel is the extended Days Between, where Jerry launches a huge solo that many listeners describe as emotionally soaring; it sits beside a lively Iko Iko and a superb sequence of That Would Be Something → Drum Solo → Days Between → Throwing Stones that lifts the entire concert. While the first half drifts at times, moments like Picasso Moon, Samson & Delilah, and a tight Truckin' keep the set from sagging completely. The encore’s U.S. Blues offers a familiar, upbeat send‑off.\n\nFrom an archival perspective the audience tape (gd94-10-02.pmb.pujol.15111.sbeok.shnf) provides clear, well‑balanced sound that captures these peaks without major dropouts, making it the go‑to source for this show. Listeners seeking the emotional high of Days Between and a lively second set will find this recording the most rewarding, even if the overall energy feels uneven.",
